Optional linked or compile-time dependencies
--------------------------------------------

The source package does not redistribute the following dependency trees or
shared libraries. configure enables them only when their installed headers and
libraries are found or explicitly requested. Exact installed versions belong
in the build and hardware-validation manifest.

* RAPIDS cuVS (Apache-2.0): optional libcuvs_c/libcuvs linkage for CUDA
  exact and IVF-Flat search. License copy: LICENSES/CUVS-LICENSE.
* RAPIDS RAFT (Apache-2.0): optional installed TSVD headers and runtime
  dependencies for resident CUDA PCA initialization.
* RAPIDS RMM and rapids-logger (Apache-2.0): linked only with the optional
  RAFT route.
* NVIDIA CCCL CUB/Thrust headers: supplied by the CUDA toolkit or RAPIDS
  environment and compiled into CUDA translation units under their upstream
  Apache-2.0/LLVM-exception, BSD, and Boost terms.
* NVIDIA CUDA Toolkit: external cudart, cuFFT, cuBLAS, cuSOLVER, cuSPARSE,
  cuRAND, and nvJitLink libraries under the NVIDIA CUDA Toolkit license.

No cuML or cuGraph library, Python module, or runtime symbol is linked or
called by the installed package.

Apple system frameworks
-----------------------

On supported Apple Silicon systems, configure links Foundation, Accelerate,
Metal, MetalPerformanceShaders, and MetalPerformanceShadersGraph from the
installed macOS/Xcode SDK. These Apple system frameworks are not redistributed
in fastEmbedR. The package does not redistribute MPS or MPSGraph binaries.

Independently implemented code with pinned design references
-------------------------------------------------------------

The following repositories were inspected as behavioral, mathematical, or
architecture references. They are not copied, linked, vendored, or called.

* NetworKit, commit 7b74f6af90bc0865c6c0937a206df63df331b712,
  MIT. The ParallelLeiden phase organization was reviewed while implementing
  package-owned graph storage and community detection. The full upstream
  notice is retained as LICENSES/NETWORKIT-LICENSE.
* RAPIDS cuGraph, commit 528ddde979df2243bf51c116d89a0ecdf85a39ee,
  Apache-2.0. Public CSR/parallel-processing documentation informed the
  independent CUDA/Metal clustering design; cuGraph is not a dependency.
* openTSNE, commit 12b8b7bec3d96ee0bc8930c3c45449a5209ed3e0,
  BSD-3-Clause. Mathematical and workflow reference for native sparse
  affinities, two-stage optimization, and fixed-reference transformation.
* FIt-SNE, commit 47ff14f1defc1ff3a8065c8b7baaf45c33e7e0b2,
  mixed file-specific BSD-4-Clause, MIT, Apache-2.0, and GPL-2.0-or-later
  terms. Only the published interpolation/FFT decomposition is referenced;
  no repository source is reused.
* t-SNE-CUDA, commit 44249b6895a2eb389b8a13390ed6fb125d2040c8,
  BSD-3-Clause. GPU-resident sparse-attraction/interpolated-repulsion
  architecture reference.
* umap-learn, commit f6dcf3e261bcf78aa3366d60c2a8fc4b75bf58c4,
  BSD-3-Clause. UMAP mathematical/reference-behavior comparison; no Python
  implementation source is used.
* Multicore-opt-SNE, commit c6d15e3d4c0372ea8e7f652014819c98354a3325,
  BSD-3-Clause. Automatic t-SNE parameter-policy reference.
* mlx-vis, commit 06c8a75ad007820b35185937f83c03e09ab6bd5b,
  Apache-2.0. GPU-resident buffer and kernel-organization reference.
* annembed, commit eceda8368d69e8c8790285312a974a865d063a07,
  MIT OR Apache-2.0. Landmarking and resident-buffer architecture reference.
* Rtsne, commit 0e769505ab791fa3c3ac25bd9434ff20e1f0a689,
  mixed file-specific BSD-4-Clause and BSD-3-Clause terms. Public KNN-input
  behavior and validation are references; no Barnes-Hut implementation source
  is present in fastEmbedR.

The UMAP power approximation is a package-local implementation of the
IEEE-754 exponent-interpolation idea described by Schraudolph (1999). It was
not copied from uwot or a third-party code snippet.

Benchmark-only software and repository licensing
------------------------------------------------

Rtsne, uwot, umap, igraph, Python openTSNE, FIt-SNE, umap-learn, and RAPIDS
cuML may be used by external benchmark/validation scripts. They are not
production dependencies. In particular, GPL-3.0-or-later uwot source is not
copied, linked, translated, or required by fastEmbedR.

The separate benchmark repository is
https://github.com/tkcaccia/fastEmbedR-extra and is licensed under MIT.
Its benchmark scripts do not relicense datasets or third-party programs;
dataset-specific terms remain with the original providers.

